                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "While Capsule Force does has some single player missions, for the most part the game is a multiplayer experience. If you are looking at Capsule Force as a single player game you will probably be disappointed. While I had fun with the single player missions I see them more as a training exercise for the multiplayer mode. \n\nThe multiplayer mode is where the game excels. It is hard to explain why but the game is just fun to play. The game is fast paced with both teams fighting in order to progress one of the trams towards the other team's base. Bullets will end up flying all over the screen. The game has a lot of back and forth as one team will make some progress and then the other team will regain that ground.\n\nUnfortunately at the time of this review the game doesn't appear to have online multiplayer. This is disappointing since the game would have been better since you could then have more matches with four players which are probably more fun than two player matches.\n\nIf you like fast paced multiplayer games and the concept of the game looks interesting to you, I think you will enjoy Capsule Force.\n\nNote: I received a free review copy of Capsule Force. Other than receiving the free review copy I received no other compensation for this review.\n\n[url=http://www.geekyhobbies.com/capsule-force-indie-game-review/] Read My Full Review [/url]",
